{
 "_note": [
  "Lexicon of the English curriculum, mirroring training_files/it/lexicon.json.",
  "Apostrophes are written as spaces everywhere in this corpus, so no target",
  "here uses a contraction: 'do not', never 'don t'.",
  "English has no grammatical gender, so the Italian 'g' and the m/f pair on",
  "the adjectives are gone; 'art' is the definite article ('the' for every",
  "noun) and 'indef' the indefinite one, spelled out per noun so that no a/an",
  "rule is needed.",
  "'kind' constrains which verbs and adjectives make sense with a noun: without",
  "it the generator writes 'the bread sleeps', which teaches noise.",
  "'can' lists the verbs that make sense for that noun (the Italian file calls",
  "this key 'puo'), 'verb_places' the places for each verb ('luoghi_verbo'),",
  "'dim'/'pol' the semantic dimension and the polarity of each adjective.",
  "Verbs are stored in the third person singular under 'pres', because that is",
  "the form every target uses ('the cat sleeps.'); 'base' carries the bare",
  "infinitive for the 'can' and 'want to' frames of level 1.",
  "'past' is the SIMPLE past ('the dog ate the bread.'), never the participle,",
  "because that is the one form levels 6-10 ask for. The future needs no",
  "field: it is 'will ' + 'base' for every verb.",
  "'cmp' is the comparative of an adjective, spelled out because -er versus",
  "'more' cannot be derived (good/better, happy/happier, tired/more tired).",
  "'ontology' carries the is-a relation; 'unknown_nouns' the nouns kept out of",
  "the curriculum, half of them marked 'probe'.",
  "'mass' marks mass nouns: they take no indefinite article, so they introduce",
  "themselves as 'this is water', not 'this is a water'.",
  "'uniq' marks unique referents: 'this is the sun', because 'this is a sun'",
  "is not said.",
  "There is no 'bare_unknown_nouns' block: the honesty curriculum lives at",
  "levels 11-13 and the English tree stops at level 5, so inventing roles here",
  "would only give scripts/validate_teacher_configs.py words that no level",
  "teaches.",
  "scripts/expand_teacher_pools.py does NOT read this file: its gender",
  "agreement and its elisions are Italian. The English pools are hand written."
 ],
